# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Get information on the global X.509 authentication configuration.

## Example Usage

```terraform
# Read the current global X.509 configuration
data "wallix-bastion_config_x509" "current" {}

# Check whether X509 user authentication is currently enabled
output "x509_status" {
  value = {
    enabled            = data.wallix-bastion_config_x509.current.enable
    has_ca_certificate = length(data.wallix-bastion_config_x509.current.ca_certificate) > 0
  }
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Usage Notes

### No Lookup Key

`config_x509` is a singleton: there is only one X.509 configuration on the Bastion, so this data source takes **no arguments**. It always reads that single, global configuration rather than looking anything up by name — the same configuration managed by the `wallix-bastion_config_x509` resource, internally identified by the fixed ID `x509Config`.

### Returned Attributes

- **ca_certificate**: The CA certificate used for validating client certificates presented during X.509 user authentication
- **server_public_key**: The server certificate's public key, used for the Bastion's GUI/API HTTPS endpoint
- **server_private_key**: The server certificate's private key
- **enable**: Whether X.509 user authentication is currently enabled

Because `server_private_key` is sensitive material, avoid printing it directly in outputs; treat it the same way you would treat any other credential retrieved through this provider.
